From 4e58ca877fbbfbe6f30011a0b740390a5e3895dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:35:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/43] test(chexc): cross-package serialization (10) and
 performs (4, red-first)

serialization/: every shape a capability list can take across a package
boundary -- free function, method, property accessor, generic instantiation in
both directions, a clause nested in a functional type, a capturing class, the
canonical form of the exported list, and the incremental-compilation cache.
libx.cj is a CHECKED dependency (compiled with the flag), so the negative cases
are the load-bearing ones: before the feature they compiled clean.

xpkg_captures_pos.cj is kept as a runtime sanity check but does not discriminate
on its own -- it passes either way, since the try/catch catches at runtime
whether or not a compile-time demand was raised. xpkg_captures_neg.cj is the
test that proves the metadata crossed.

performs/: red-first for proposal 8.2, per the test-first convention -- the
handler round trip, an undeclared 'perform' (which also pins that effect
requirements are NEVER inferred, where an exception in the same position would
be), non-discharge across the two capability kinds in both directions, and
'performs' entries having to be Command subtypes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
